  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Soak burghul: Put the burghul in a large heatproof bowl, add 100ml boiling water and 1 tsp olive oil (see Kitchen 101), season with salt and pepper and stir to combine. Cover the bowl with a plate and stand for 10 mins or until the water is absorbed.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2892544/photos/large/149330_1-88bc415b566b1d036d78c9d099240cda.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Meanwhile, finely chop the tomato. Finely chop the parsley leaves and stems. Finely chop the currants. Combine half the sumac, 2 tsp olive oil and 1 tsp white wine vinegar in a bowl and season with salt and pepper. Add the currants and stir to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2892545/photos/large/149330_2-145cf1650f9ba7b37bc150c5980bd8cd.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fry falafel: Combine the remaining sumac and 2 tsp honey in a bowl. Heat 2 tsp olive oil in a medium frypan over medium-high heat. Fry the falafel, turning regularly, for 3-5 mins until golden. Add the sumac mixture and cook, tossing, for 1 min or until the falafel are evenly coated. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2892546/photos/large/149330_3-987cbf55b2179a4c0949aafd98cd17e1.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make tabouleh: Crumble the feta. Stir the feta, tomato and parsley into the burghul. Add 2 tsp olive oil and 1 tsp white wine vinegar, season with salt and pepper and stir to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2892547/photos/large/149330_4-234bc1ad11c8dcb2d014793ab1fd24e3.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the hummus among bowls, spreading with the back of a spoon, then drizzle with 1 tsp olive oil. Top with the tabouleh and falafel and drizzle with the sumac and currant dressing. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2892548/photos/large/149330_5-599d087f7f6ad2d4fe8915c6d8f17d98.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen 101: Adding a little oil to the burghul when soaking adds flavour and helps to separate the grains.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2892549/photos/large/149330_6-2114d8f1526e2502d27d8a7ccc6a8def.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
